          "claim": "Wall stabilizers, (ii). The functional $f=(0,1)$ lies in $C$ with $f(e_s)=0$ and $f(e_t)=1$, so $S(f)=\\{s\\}$ and the stabilizer formula gives $\\operatorname{Stab}_W(f)=W_{\\{s\\}}=\\{1,s\\}$; every point of the open face $C_{\\{s\\}}=\\{x_s=0,\\ x_t>0\\}$ has the same zero set $\\{s\\}$, so the same formula applies to all of them, and symmetrically every point of $C_{\\{t\\}}=\\{x_t=0,\\ x_s>0\\}$ has stabilizer $\\{1,t\\}$.",
          "step": "1.2",
